w latency.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact on Network Performance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Effective separation of data and power cables directly contributes to maintaining and improving overall 'DESEMPENHO DA REDE' (Network Performance) [Data: Entities (215), Relationships (290)]. Electromagnetic interference can slow down data transmission, increase latency, and cause packet loss, all of which degrade network performance [Data: Entities (215)]. By mitigating these interferences, the separation principle ensures that networks operate at their intended speeds and efficiencies [Data: Relationships (290)]. This is vital for businesses and organizations that rely on robust and high-performing networks for their operations.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Implementation Challenges: Space and Route Planning\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Implementing the 'SEPARAÇÃO DE CABOS DE DADOS E ENERGIA' is not without its challenges. A significant consideration is the requirement for adequate 'ESPAÇO' (Space) to maintain the necessary physical separation between cable types [Data: Entities (235), Relationships (306)]. Furthermore, the planning of 'ROTAS' (Routes) for cable installation becomes more complex [Data: Entities (220), Relationships (308)]. Detailed 'PLANOS DE INSTALAÇÃO' (Installation Plans) and 'PLANOS DE ROTAS' (Route Plans) are crucial to ensure that data and power cables are correctly segregated throughout their paths [Data: Entities (236), Entities (237), Relationships (322), Relationships (323)]. This careful planning can lead to more intricate and potentially costly 'INFRAESTRUTURA DE ENCAMINHAMENTO' (Routing Infrastructure) [Data: Entities (141), Relationships (214)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Application in Commercial and Industrial Environments\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The principle of separating data and power cables finds its primary application in 'EDIFÍCIOS 